{
  "format": "satk.kit-blanks-automobile/1",
  "_comment": [
    "Body profiles of the automobile blank (kit.blank --kind automobile). Our own parametric construction:",
    "proportions in fractions of the length L (t = 0 rear end .. 1 front end) and of the height H above the ground,",
    "centred on the class medians of the style guides; no vanilla vertex, face or texture is used anywhere.",
    "top/belt/floor are centre-line profiles [[t, h]]; crease_t lists the knots with a tangent break.",
    "A tier's profile holds defaults (density, crown, details); a body's own values win over them.",
    "Optional stations: tailgate (hatch/bed bodies: the tail panel belongs to the boot part), quarter_rear and",
    "quarter_front (fixed side glass behind the rear door), bed_front (the open bed of a pickup).",
    "like_body: vanilla model name -> body when --like names it (else the style class of the model)."
